  "message": "I checked with toyota_mechanic: **DIAGNOSIS (nothing changed):** The pause isn't between real sentences — it's happening after *any* period, including abbreviations like \"Jan.\", \"Inc.\", \"e.g.\" that are common in finance replies. The sentence-splitter treats those as sentence boundaries too, so each one gets the same 0.35s inter-sentence pause.\n\n**Smallest fix identified:** tighten the sentence-split regex to only break on a period followed by whitespace + an uppercase letter/quote/end-of-string, so abbreviation periods no longer trigger a false sentence boundary. No files were changed — this was diagnose-only.",
